1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,980
=Episode 2=

15
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:12,660
(Shen Manor)

16
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:33,120
My character's dowry isn't much.

17
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,070
I'll have to find a way

18
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:37,230
to make more money.

19
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:39,280
I didn't expect
the Heir's wife to be so capable.

20
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:41,400
She actually foiled
First Madam's scheme.

21
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,040
She just got lucky.

22
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:45,130
If she hadn't

23
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:46,480
coveted the title
of the Marquis's Heir's Wife

24
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:47,450
and forced her way
into the Marquis's Manor,

25
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,000
no one would have plotted against her.

26
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:49,950
(Sanqi, the Heir's Secret Guard)

27
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:50,580
When all is said and done,

28
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:52,280
she's still a fool.

29
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,640
(Are you out of your mind?)

30
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,840
(You're the fool!)

31
00:01:57,070 --> 00:01:58,280
(Your whole family's full of fools!)

32
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,310
Your Lordship,
the poison is acting up again.

33
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:03,750
Luckily, we've prepared the antidote.

34
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:04,780
Please take it now.

35
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,940
Did I just jinx him?

36
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:09,900
He really is poisoned.

37
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:15,960
What are you doing here?

38
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:16,840
Speak.

39
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:18,140
How much did you hear?

40
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,470
Let go of me...

41
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,240
There's only one fate

42
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,400
for those who know my secret.

43
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:24,840
Death.

44
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:26,910
(I don't want to know

45
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:28,190
(your stupid secret, man.)

46
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:35,800
- My Lady.
- Stay back!

47
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,810
- My La...
- Nobody come any closer.

48
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,240
Aren't you poisoned?

49
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,310
If you want me dead,

50
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,120
you're coming with me!

51
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:46,870
Spit it out.

52
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,310
If I'm going to die anyway,

53
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:02,380
I might as well take you with me.

54
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:04,280
Worth it.

55
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,360
(I'm still alive?)

56
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,440
Your Lordship,

57
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:20,110
well...

58
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,150
The antidote has entered
her bloodstream.

59
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:23,890
Until a new antidote can be made,

60
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,480
if you wish to suppress the poison,

61
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,880
you'll need to use her blood

62
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,360
in your medicine every ten days.

63
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,740
(What kind of outdated
melodramatic plot is this?)

64
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:34,930
(Stupid mouth.)

65
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:35,910
(That's what you get
for swallowing random stuff.)

66
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,230
(Now you're his personal
walking blood bank.)

67
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:38,820
And...

68
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:39,430
And there's more.

69
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,360
Speak.

70
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:41,630
She

71
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:43,280
must stay cheerful

72
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:44,430
and maintain healthy blood circulation.

73
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,240
That will make her blood

74
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:47,680
more effective in the medicine.

75
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,360
(I take back what I just said.)

76
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:51,840
(People who love to eat

77
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:53,230
(really are lucky after all.)

78
00:03:53,470 --> 00:03:54,750
(Love you, my dear mouth.)

79
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:55,550
You mean

80
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,710
not only am I dependent on her now,

81
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:59,060
but I also have to keep her happy?

82
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:03,840
(Bestie,)

83
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:06,780
(good times are coming our way.)

84
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:07,960
(From now on,)

85
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:10,910
(I'll rule the Marquis's Manor.)

86
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,960
(Let's see who dares upset me.)

87
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,600
I do have another solution.

88
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,560
Build an ice cellar.

89
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,630
Before she gets upset,

90
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,480
drain every drop of blood from her body.

91
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,190
Your Lordship,

92
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:36,280
what are you saying?

93
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:39,620
I'm actually

94
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,180
very good at keeping myself happy.

95
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,120
I eat when I'm hungry

96
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,690
and head home when it rains.

97
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:47,540
Well,

98
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,500
I'll leave you to talk.

99
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:49,830
My alarm's going off.

100
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:50,750
I need to answer a call.

101
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:56,430
What's a phone call?

102
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,460
Why does she seem

103
00:04:58,950 --> 00:04:59,620
like a different person?

104
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,480
She's just afraid of dying.

105
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:02,960
Keep an eye on her.

106
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,230
As for Shen He,

107
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:07,120
has he been acting strangely lately?

108
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,070
The Third Young Master

109
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:09,040
has been frequenting brothels lately,

110
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,120
staying there all day.

111
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:11,120
I've heard

112
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:12,510
he's also spent a fortune

113
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:13,920
on some rather strange items.

114
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:25,000
No, no.

115
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:26,560
These are all outdated.

116
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,800
(Cangzhu, Third Young Master's Attendant)
Money's no object.

117
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,920
Order me a new batch.

118
00:05:29,190 --> 00:05:29,600
They must

119
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,630
fit my hands perfectly.

120
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:33,870
Also,

121
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:35,510
order me a batch of silver needles

122
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:37,750
and some red wax.

123
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,040
(Silver needles?)

124
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:40,140
(Red wax?)

125
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,190
(He's into such twisted things?)

126
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:43,720
(That's not being a playboy.)

127
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,160
(That's downright indecent.)

128
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:45,760
Young Master,

129
00:05:46,070 --> 00:05:46,870
aren't you worried

130
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:47,480
about Third Madam?

131
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,930
I heard that last night,

132
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,310
First Madam had her drugged
and taken away.

133
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:51,800
She must have suffered terribly.

134
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,120
Xiang acted far too quickly.

135
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:55,240
What a shame.

136
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:59,100
I didn't even get to use

137
00:05:59,310 --> 00:06:00,430
the liquor I specially prepared for her.

138
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:03,290
(What a sick man.)

139
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,790
(I'll teach you a lesson.)

140
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,600
Have I kept you waiting, Dear?

141
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:10,160
Madam.

142
00:06:17,930 --> 00:06:18,660
It's not too late

143
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,310
to drink the liquor now.

144
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,430
You're that eager to have me?

145
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,270
Fine.

146
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:30,360
In that case,

147
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,190
let's finally enjoy

148
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:33,600
our wedding night.

149
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:36,750
No problem.

150
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:47,680
You...

151
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:58,830
What...

152
00:06:59,360 --> 00:06:59,940
What are you doing?

153
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,160
Whatever you wanted to do to me,

154
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,450
I'm doing to you.

155
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,400
Give me back the antidote.

156
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:14,750
Lin Shutiao,

157
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,270
how dare you treat me like this?

158
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,040
Don't you believe

159
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,860
I'll divorce you?

160
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:20,870
Divorce me?

161
00:07:21,510 --> 00:07:22,870
Wouldn't that make my life

162
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:24,160
wonderfully carefree?

163
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:25,480
A shameless,

164
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:27,240
ill-mannered, immoral man like you

165
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:29,040
still wants the antidote?

166
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,120
You...

167
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:31,680
Take that as a lesson.

168
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,680
I think you might have...

169
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:52,120
I'm fine.

170
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:53,560
Wasn't the antidote

171
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:55,680
destroyed?

172
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,320
To be precise,

173
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:58,740
only half was destroyed.

174
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,130
What does that mean?

175
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,830
Rectal administration.

176
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:15,720
Twice the effectiveness?

177
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:21,020
(Rectal Administration,
Twice the Effectiveness)

178
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:22,750
Be gentle.

179
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,720
Those two wretched women

180
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:29,240
actually dared
to humiliate me in public.

181
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:31,510
If they ever receive noble titles

182
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:33,750
and take charge of the Marquis's Manor,

183
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:35,840
won't they walk all over me?

184
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:38,860
Xiang, don't be angry just yet.

185
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,830
Since they escaped last night,

186
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,660
they must already suspect something.

187
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:44,360
We can't afford

188
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:45,470
to act rashly again.

189
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:47,630
I'm not that foolish.

190
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:48,750
Xiangchun,

191
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:51,300
go teach

192
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,770
those two new brides
some proper manners.

193
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,950
Make them understand

194
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:56,910
whether they're capable
of challenging me.

195
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:57,910
Yes, Madam.

196
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,310
Who's she?

197
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:06,730
Why is she so arrogant?

198
00:09:07,190 --> 00:09:08,680
She's Xiang's

199
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:10,260
most trusted lackey.

200
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,390
She's the one who

201
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:12,750
suggested the scheme to Xiang last night

202
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:14,550
to frame our characters for adultery.

203
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:15,550
Silence!

204
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:17,910
Here,

205
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:21,270
there are rules
for every movement you make.

206
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,150
Your first lesson

207
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:24,210
is serving tea.

208
00:09:24,510 --> 00:09:26,040
When serving tea,

209
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:27,750
your hands must be steady

210
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,080
and your heart sincere.

211
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:32,750
Spilling water shows a restless heart.

212
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,900
If the tea goes cold,

213
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,290
it shows a lack of sincerity.

214
00:09:39,470 --> 00:09:40,140
Pour the tea.

215
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:56,260
How...

216
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,320
How is this possible?

217
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:58,840
You...

218
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:02,910
Wow.

219
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,630
So it's true that a dead pig

220
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:05,960
fears no boiling water.

221
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,500
How dare you insult me?

222
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:08,870
Let's see

223
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:09,840
what tricks you two are playing.

224
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:14,240
Hey.

225
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,410
When I said
a dead pig fears no boiling water,

226
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,360
I was talking about that pig.

227
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,590
You took it personally, didn't you?

228
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:22,870
You...

229
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:23,720
I was planning

230
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,100
to stew it for lunch today.

231
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,760
Having you scald the hair off it

232
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:28,990
is quite an honor
for this pig's trotter.

233
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,000
How dare you make a fool of me?

234
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,000
If you hadn't

235
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,910
run away so quickly last night,

236
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:39,750
you'd have been drowned in the pond

237
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:40,750
along with the man.

238
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:42,130
That man from last night

239
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,320
was brought there by you.

240
00:10:43,430 --> 00:10:43,750
Don't...

241
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:44,980
Don't make false accusations.

242
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,470
You two were clearly

243
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,250
the ones behaving shamelessly

244
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:48,720
and fooling around

245
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,390
with some disreputable man.

246
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,600
Besides,

247
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,990
it takes two to tango!

248
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,130
Wow.

249
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:58,840
That was quite a loud slap.

250
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,400
How dare you slap me?

251
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,550
I slapped you

252
00:11:02,550 --> 00:11:03,510
because I have a poor memory.

253
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:04,670
I can't remember whether

254
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:05,980
I've already shown you enough respect.

255
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,320
I'm First Madam's

256
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:10,970
most beautiful attendant, you know?

257
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:12,490
Everyone here

258
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,520
has to show me respect.

259
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:16,120
As long as it's within this manor,

260
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:18,440
even if I wanted the stars in the sky,

261
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:20,200
they'd find a way to get them for me.

262
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,640
You? First Madam?

263
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:25,540
Who do you think you are?

264
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:26,760
I'm warning you.

265
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:28,660
Stay away from us from now on.

266
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:31,350
We have a fear of clusters.

267
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,200
We can't stand being around people

268
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,140
with too many schemes up their sleeves.

269
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:37,510
That's enough, Yuyuan.

270
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,710
This lady is getting on in years.

271
00:11:40,030 --> 00:11:41,320
We should show her some respect.

272
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:42,150
Alright.

273
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:46,480
You want to see stars, right?

274
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:52,630
What are you going to do?

275
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:53,390
Of course,

276
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:55,880
we're going to show you some stars.

277
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:58,780
Starfish.

278
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,670
Mercury.

279
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:00,820
Saturn.

280
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,800
You've really made me proud.

281
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,120
You got chased around

282
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,220
and beaten with pig trotters
by those two wretches,

283
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,840
and you still have the nerve
to come crying to me?

284
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,660
They

285
00:12:13,660 --> 00:12:14,960
were just too cunning.

286
00:12:15,090 --> 00:12:16,320
First Madam, you must

287
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,930
stand up for me.

288
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,320
They haven't even taken charge
of the household,

289
00:12:22,630 --> 00:12:23,550
yet they already dare to attack

290
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:24,960
your most trusted attendant, Xiang.

291
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:27,150
They weren't just attacking Xiangchun.

292
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:28,440
They were trying

293
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,480
to intimidate you.

294
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:34,550
They think my ten years
of household scheming were for nothing?

295
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:36,750
Xiangchun,

296
00:12:37,390 --> 00:12:38,510
starting today,

297
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:39,840
keep a close eye on them.

298
00:12:40,550 --> 00:12:41,960
I refuse to believe

299
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,000
we won't find something
to use against them.

300
00:12:47,790 --> 00:12:49,180
You've got pig liver

301
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:50,310
and red date cakes.

302
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:51,550
Anyone who didn't know better
would think

303
00:12:51,550 --> 00:12:52,440
you were recovering from childbirth.

304
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:53,750
You think I want this?

305
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,030
That awful man

306
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:56,240
puts me through this

307
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,300
every ten days.

308
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,250
Every ten days, you know?

309
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,360
Tonight's the night again.

310
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:03,220
If I don't eat more,

311
00:13:03,390 --> 00:13:05,320
how will my poor body take it?

312
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:07,960
Well, well.

313
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,750
We failed to frame you

314
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:10,870
on the pleasure boat last time.

315
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,240
Now you've walked right into our trap.

316
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:16,910
My Lady.

317
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:18,630
My Lady.

318
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:19,600
Third Madam.

319
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:21,320
The Heir's poison suddenly flared up

320
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,150
on his way back to the manor.

321
00:13:22,150 --> 00:13:23,240
His carriage is outside right now.

322
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,320
Please help him.

323
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,660
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

324
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:37,860
♪Right now,
I just want to stay by your side♪

325
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:43,060
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

326
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:49,300
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

327
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:55,760
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

328
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:02,220
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

329
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,890
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

330
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:28,990
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
